    "narrative": "As we navigate the final stretch of the 2026 campaign, the Austin Waves remain laser-focused on optimizing our 5x5 production, particularly in the stolen base category where our roster's high-sprint-speed profiles remain our primary engine. Today, our starting lineup is anchored by **Brayan Rocchio**, who carries a score of 43.06 against Peralta. While **Brayan Rocchio** sits at the bottom of the order\u2014a significant drag on his run-production potential\u2014his matchup against a mediocre 4.32 xERA arm and his recent form provide a marginal baseline that justifies his inclusion to preserve our efficiency caps. We are balancing these daily starts carefully, as the remainder of our high-impact core, including **Kyle Tucker** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, are inactive today due to the schedule, and **Luis Robert Jr.** continues his recovery on the IL.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s board was bypassing **Liam Hicks**, who finished with a score of 31.07. While **Liam Hicks** offered some utility, he failed to cross our 40-point \"Zebras Floor.\" His matchup against Messick (3.51 xERA) presented a clear disadvantage, with the L-vs-L platoon penalty and the restrictive nature of an #8 batting order assignment effectively capping his ceiling. By benching **Liam Hicks** and maintaining our strict threshold, we prioritize potential over raw volume, ensuring we don't bleed points in AVG or waste a game cap on a low-probability output. With the rest of our depth\u2014including **Gunnar Henderson**, **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Henry Bolte**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Franklin Arias**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Luis Lara**\u2014managing their respective rests, we remain positioned to maximize our efficiency metrics through the final buzzer.",
